node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# The `.env` for a datasources.d/-based deployment: server keys + token grants only,
# no DS_* blocks. Tracked as a template alongside .env.example, which documents the
# other layout. Holds placeholders only — real credentials go in `.env`, still ignored.
!.env.multi.example
# Datasource credential files. The .env patterns above match on BASENAME, and
# `warehouse.env` starts with neither ".env" nor ".env." — so without this line the
# feature's own credential files would be committable by default.
#
# `datasources.d/*`, NOT `datasources.d/`: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the directory form would silently swallow the negation
# below and the tracked template with it. Verified both ways with `git check-ignore`.
datasources.d/*
!datasources.d/example.env.disabled
.DS_Store
docs/risks/
.ai-devkit.json
# Local agent tooling. `.claude/*`, NOT `.claude/`, for the same reason as
# `datasources.d/*` above: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is
# excluded, and `.claude/agent-memory/code-reviewer/` is TRACKED — four writeups of
# real guard bypasses that CLAUDE.md tells contributors to read before touching the
# guards. The directory form would silently swallow the negation, so a fifth writeup
# would never become committable. Verified both ways with `git check-ignore`.
.claude/*
!.claude/agent-memory/
